      title: 'Corporate website mistakes that make you lose clients',
      meta: 'Published on March 2, 2026 · 5 min read',
      body: `<p class="intro-lead">A website can look good and still fail commercially. The problem is not always visual. Many businesses lose contacts because the message is confusing, navigation gets in the way or the next step for the user is unclear.</p><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>It is not immediately clear what the company does</li><li>The structure confuses instead of guiding</li><li>Calls to action are weak or missing</li><li>The mobile experience is poor</li><li>The site does not build enough trust</li></ul><h2>Why they matter so much</h2><p>An effective corporate website does more than show information. It filters, persuades and makes contact easier. When it fails in those areas, it stops being a commercial asset and becomes just a digital brochure.</p><div class="highlight-box"><p><strong>A poorly focused website does not always fail with an obvious mistake.</strong> Sometimes it simply cools the user down until the opportunity disappears.</p></div><p>At <a href="https://jjodevelopers.cloud/" style="color:#60a5fa;">JJO</a> we approach corporate websites with clarity, structure and conversion in mind so they truly support the business.</p><div class="cta-section"><p>Want to review whether your current website is losing opportunities?</p><a href="https://jjodevelopers.cloud/" class="btn-cta">Visit JJO</a></div>`
