      title: 'Why a professional website is still key for a business',
      meta: 'Published on March 2, 2026 · 5 min read',
      body: `<p class="intro-lead">Many companies have social media accounts, a Google profile or marketplace listings, but none of that replaces a professional website they own. Your website is still the place where you control the message, build trust and turn visits into real contacts.</p><h2>Your website is your digital base</h2><p>Social media depends on algorithms. Ads depend on budget. A website is an asset that belongs to your business and can be improved over time.</p><ul><li>It builds credibility</li><li>It explains services clearly</li><li>It supports search visibility</li><li>It gives you a measurable contact channel</li><li>It can grow with new pages and content</li></ul><div class="highlight-box"><p><strong>A professional website is not a decorative extra.</strong> It is a commercial, positioning and trust tool. That is why it remains one of the most basic and profitable digital investments for a business.</p></div><p>At <a href="https://jjodevelopers.cloud/" style="color:#60a5fa;">JJO</a> we build websites designed to represent the business well and support real goals, not just “be online”.</p><div class="cta-section"><p>Want a website that explains your business better and helps you capture more opportunities?</p><a href="https://jjodevelopers.cloud/" class="btn-cta">Visit JJO</a></div>`
